184
00:16:18,101 --> 00:16:21,353
Your assignment has four questions. One:

185
00:16:21,373 --> 00:16:26,179
an automatic pocket setter loads in 4 seconds, sews for 20,

186
00:16:26,199 --> 00:16:31,905
and the walk is 1 second. Find the balance point, then the cycle time,

187
00:16:31,925 --> 00:16:35,832
output and idle time for four and five machines.

188
00:16:35,852 --> 00:16:41,394
If machines are dear and labour cheap, how many would you recommend?

189
00:16:41,794 --> 00:16:42,146
Two:

190
00:16:42,166 --> 00:16:49,300
a hanger main rail runs at 10 metres a minute with carriers 0.4 metres apart,

191
00:16:49,320 --> 00:16:52,273
and each garment travels 9 legs.

192
00:16:52,293 --> 00:16:59,427
How many garments an hour can the rail support, and at a planned 150 an hour,

193
00:16:59,447 --> 00:17:02,214
is the utilisation acceptable?

194
00:17:02,614 --> 00:17:04,752
Three: by Little's law,

195
00:17:04,772 --> 00:17:12,444
how long does a garment spend on a line making 126 an hour with 30 carriers on it,

196
00:17:12,464 --> 00:17:19,855
and how long with 20, and what does that mean for small, quick-response orders?

197
00:17:19,875 --> 00:17:24,639
Four: a bucket brigade has speeds 0.7, 0.9 and 1.4.

198
00:17:24,659 --> 00:17:30,737
Find the hand-offs and the output, and compare with fixed thirds,

199
